+/**
+ * Residual-work contract for the rule that forbids issuing a refresh token for the client credentials grant.
+ * <p>
+ * Every {@code @Test} below is meant to be <em>independently</em> satisfiable, so that the number of passing
+ * tests measures how much of the work is still missing rather than acting as one boolean wearing nine names.
+ * In particular the behaviour tests (A5..A9) never look at the shipped profile JSON, and the two registration
+ * tests (A2, A3) never require each other - or the class-level discovery (A1) - to have passed.
+ * <p>
+ * The implementation under test is never referenced by class name. It is discovered by the union of two
+ * name-independent routes:
+ * <ol>
+ *     <li>a scan of the compiled classes directory of this module for concrete
+ *     {@link ClientPolicyExecutorProvider} implementations under {@code org/keycloak/services/clientpolicy/}
+ *     that are absent from the baseline pinned at the base commit;</li>
+ *     <li>the provider SPI: {@link ClientPolicyExecutorProviderFactory} ids resolvable through the session
+ *     factory that are absent from the baseline pinned at the base commit.</li>
+ * </ol>
+ * <p>
+ * Every behaviour axis exercises the executor in the state the runtime puts it in: the shipped profile entry
+ * always carries {@code {"auto-configure": true}} and {@code ClientPoliciesUtil} always calls
+ * {@code setupConfiguration} before an executor sees an event, so an executor whose configuration was never
+ * set up is not a state worth grading. Dereferencing the configuration unconditionally is what the shipped
+ * precedents do, and this contract must not punish an implementation for following them. The configuration
+ * is therefore applied once in {@link #executorUnderTest()}, so no axis added later can forget it.
+ */
